We sit at the dining table together.
The food is very delicious.
Priya says, "Maya, eat this hot Varan Bhaat."
I also take some spicy Batata Bhaji.
I say, "Priya, this food is wonderful."
She smiles and says, "Thank you, I will make it for you again."
We stop talking about office work.
We talk about our personal lives.
Priya asks, "Maya, who all is in your family in Mexico?"
I tell her that my parents live there.
I have an older brother Diego and a younger sister Sofia.
I also tell her about my dog Lola.
Priya says, "I think that your family is very lovely."
Then Priya tells me about her childhood.
She says that she has always lived in Mumbai.
We eat our food slowly and talk a lot.
I think that Priya is a very good friend of mine now.
Priya smiles and says, "Let's eat dessert now."
